<given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Decisions to get HIV tested and to accept antiretroviral therapies among gay/bisexual men: implications for secondary prevention efforts.</article-title><source>J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>151</fpage><lpage>160</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000411-Liu1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanton</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Fang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Relation of sexual risks and prevention practices with individuals' stigmatising beliefs towards HIV infected individuals: an exploratory study.</article-title><source>Sex Transm Infect</source><volume>81(6)</volume><fpage>511</fpage><lpage>516</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16326857</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000411-Botnick1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Botnick</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Part 2: Fear of contagion, fear of intimacy.</article-title><source>J Homosex</source><volume>39</volume><fpage>77</fpage><lpage>101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10807029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000411-Burkholder1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burkholder</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Harlow</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Washkwich</surname><given-names>J-L</given-names><